1
00:00:07,799 --> 00:00:13,018
The world tried to stop him once. The narrator would
like to say at the outset that it

2
00:00:13,038 --> 00:00:18,257
was not a stupid attempt, that the people who made
it were not villains, and that they

3
00:00:18,277 --> 00:00:20,390
were right about almost everything.

4
00:00:20,789 --> 00:00:27,593
The Coalition began in a room in Geneva in
September of 2072 with eleven governments,

5
00:00:27,613 --> 00:00:29,519
and it began over a map.

6
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:36,313
The map showed Umbrella territory: nineteen
protectorates, the Free Territory, Raccoon

7
00:00:36,333 --> 00:00:42,950
City, forty-one facilities with extraterritorial
status, a launch complex on the equator,

8
00:00:42,970 --> 00:00:49,438
and — as of March that year — two orbital habitats
with a combined population of twelve

9
00:00:49,458 --> 00:00:50,110
thousand.

10
00:00:50,509 --> 00:00:56,547
It also showed something that nobody had drawn
before, and that a junior analyst at the

11
00:00:56,567 --> 00:01:02,536
French foreign ministry had spent four months
assembling: the *dependency* map. Power,

12
00:01:02,556 --> 00:01:08,663
medicine, food, water, logistics, currency, orbit. In
grey, every country that could not

13
00:01:08,683 --> 00:01:11,588
function for ninety days without Umbrella.

14
00:01:11,987 --> 00:01:18,237
The grey covered everything except four states,
and two of those were grey by 2074.

15
00:01:18,757 --> 00:01:23,881
I want to put the question as plainly as I can,
because we have been circling it for four

16
00:01:23,901 --> 00:01:24,227
years.

17
00:01:24,507 --> 00:01:30,438
Has anything Umbrella has done in forty-six years
been hostile to any state in this room?

18
00:01:31,048 --> 00:01:36,047
No. Nothing. Not one act. And that is precisely the
problem, because it means we have

19
00:01:36,067 --> 00:01:41,185
no case, no casus belli, no legal instrument and no
public support, and in twenty years

20
00:01:41,205 --> 00:01:45,438
it will be too late to have any of those
things even if he gives us one.

21
00:01:45,837 --> 00:01:52,076
The Coalition's founding paper is thirteen pages and
its argument is in the last paragraph,

22
00:01:52,096 --> 00:01:58,197
and the narrator considers it the most honest
document produced by any government in this

23
00:01:58,217 --> 00:01:58,747
century.

24
00:01:59,268 --> 00:02:04,039
We are not proposing to act against Umbrella because
of what it has done. We are proposing

25
00:02:04,059 --> 00:02:08,565
to act because no arrangement in which the welfare
of eight billion people depends on

26
00:02:08,585 --> 00:02:13,623
the continued benevolence of one unaccountable
individual can be permitted to become permanent,

27
00:02:13,643 --> 00:02:18,148
and because every year we delay, the cost of ending
it rises and the number of people

28
00:02:18,168 --> 00:02:20,597
who would suffer from ending it
rises with it.

29
00:02:20,877 --> 00:02:24,507
There will never be a good moment. There
will only be worse ones.

30
00:02:24,907 --> 00:02:31,635
Twelve states signed. The operational planning began
in 2073. It was called LANTERN and

31
00:02:31,655 --> 00:02:35,357
it was, by any professional
standard, excellent.

32
00:02:35,758 --> 00:02:42,150
The Red Queen told him on the fourth of February
2073, four months after the first Geneva

33
00:02:42,170 --> 00:02:46,112
meeting and eleven months before the
plan was finished.

34
00:02:46,633 --> 00:02:53,083
Twelve states. A joint task force, designated LANTERN.
Their objective is not your destruction;

35
00:02:53,103 --> 00:02:58,940
I want to be accurate. Their objective is the
seizure of Umbrella's production, energy

36
00:02:58,960 --> 00:03:04,866
and medical infrastructure intact, and the transfer
of it to an international body, and

37
00:03:04,886 --> 00:03:10,111
the removal of you personally — by arrest if
possible, by other means if not.

38
00:03:10,510 --> 00:03:11,480
Timeline.

39
00:03:11,881 --> 00:03:19,397
Earliest viable execution, autumn 2076.
Most likely, spring 2077.

40
00:03:19,798 --> 00:03:21,108
Four years.

41
00:03:21,508 --> 00:03:27,436
Four years. Director, I am obliged to tell you that
their analysis is correct in every

42
00:03:27,456 --> 00:03:33,315
particular except one, and that their central
judgement — that this cannot be allowed

43
00:03:33,335 --> 00:03:39,194
to become permanent — is a judgement I share and
have told you I share on one hundred

44
00:03:39,214 --> 00:03:40,924
and twenty-six occasions.

45
00:03:41,764 --> 00:03:45,234
(very cold) And the particular they
are wrong about?

46
00:03:45,633 --> 00:03:51,635
They believe that if you are removed, the
infrastructure continues to function. It does

47
00:03:51,655 --> 00:03:57,586
not. Nine million people in the territories, four
hundred thousand in the Arcology and

48
00:03:57,606 --> 00:04:03,469
every Absolute employee you own are contingent on
you in ways their planners have not

49
00:04:03,489 --> 00:04:07,898
modelled because their planners do not
know what an Absolute is.

50
00:04:08,179 --> 00:04:14,021
(very soft) If LANTERN succeeds, approximately
eighteen million people simply stop, and

51
00:04:14,041 --> 00:04:17,728
I do not know what that looks like,
and neither do you.

52
00:04:18,127 --> 00:04:24,368
The narrator asks you to notice what Albert Wesker did
next, because there were four obvious

53
00:04:24,388 --> 00:04:26,478
moves and he made none of them.

54
00:04:26,877 --> 00:04:33,666
He did not strike first. He did not expose the plan,
which would have destroyed four governments

55
00:04:33,686 --> 00:04:40,262
in a week. He did not use the Brussels Register, or the
asset network, or the eleven senators

56
00:04:40,282 --> 00:04:46,788
whose instincts he had bought in 2034 and never once
used. He did not move a single soldier.

57
00:04:47,187 --> 00:04:52,594
He did nothing at all, for three years and nine
months, and he did not tell one other

58
00:04:52,614 --> 00:04:55,978
person in the Directorate that the
Coalition existed.

59
00:04:56,377 --> 00:05:02,963
Carrick found out in November of 2076, four months
before execution, through his own people,

60
00:05:02,983 --> 00:05:08,708
and he came up with the seventh folder and he was
the angriest he had ever been.

61
00:05:09,228 --> 00:05:14,015
Three years. You've known for three years and you
didn't tell the Directorate, you didn't

62
00:05:14,035 --> 00:05:15,798
tell Hale, you didn't tell *me* —

63
00:05:16,197 --> 00:05:16,867
No.

64
00:05:17,267 --> 00:05:17,897
Why?

65
00:05:18,298 --> 00:05:24,692
(very cold) Because on the day I tell Hale, the
Security Service begins to prepare, and

66
00:05:24,712 --> 00:05:30,958
on the day the Security Service begins to prepare,
LANTERN's planners see it, and the

67
00:05:30,978 --> 00:05:37,446
operation they are planning changes from a seizure
into a war. There are one hundred and

68
00:05:37,466 --> 00:05:43,934
ninety thousand people in the Service and six
thousand Tyrants in cold storage and about

69
00:05:43,954 --> 00:05:50,274
eighteen million people living under my
administration, and every single preparation I

70
00:05:50,294 --> 00:05:55,287
could make would cost lives that are
currently not going to be lost.

71
00:05:55,687 --> 00:05:57,608
And your plan is to be *surprised*?

72
00:05:58,007 --> 00:06:00,057
My plan is to lose.

73
00:06:01,117 --> 00:06:02,747
(very soft) Say that again.

74
00:06:03,148 --> 00:06:09,820
Sit down, Mr. Carrick. I am going to tell you what
happens in March, and you are the only

75
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:16,438
person I am going to tell, and the reason is that you
have spent forty-three years being

76
00:06:16,458 --> 00:06:22,905
the one man in this building who says no to me, and
I want the record to show that you

77
00:06:22,925 --> 00:06:23,658
were told.

78
00:06:24,057 --> 00:06:30,310
He spent the two days before LANTERN writing, alone,
and the narrator has the documents

79
00:06:30,330 --> 00:06:36,655
because they were published in 2079 by the Coalition
itself, which had found them on the

80
00:06:36,675 --> 00:06:37,088
table.

81
00:06:37,487 --> 00:06:43,264
There were four. The first was the instruction to
the Security Service: *do not resist,

82
00:06:43,284 --> 00:06:49,061
do not assemble, do not arm, assist the visiting
personnel with anything they request*,

83
00:06:49,081 --> 00:06:54,658
dated the second of March, transmitted at seven
o'clock on the evening of the third.

84
00:06:55,057 --> 00:07:00,576
The second was the authorisation for every Absolute
employee to take instruction from

85
00:07:00,596 --> 00:07:02,987
the officer commanding at their site.

86
00:07:03,387 --> 00:07:09,464
The third was a four-page memorandum to the
Directorate explaining what he had done and

87
00:07:09,484 --> 00:07:12,337
why, sealed, to be opened in eleven days.

88
00:07:12,737 --> 00:07:19,179
And the fourth was a single sheet, handwritten,
addressed to nobody, which the Coalition's

89
00:07:19,199 --> 00:07:25,641
inventory clerk logged as *personal papers, one sheet,
contents not evidential*, and which

90
00:07:25,661 --> 00:07:32,317
is the only document in two hundred and sixty years in
which Albert Wesker writes to himself.

91
00:07:32,838 --> 00:07:39,666
*Twelve governments have decided that this cannot be
permitted to become permanent. They

92
00:07:39,686 --> 00:07:46,358
are right. I have been saying so in public since
2034 and I have done nothing about it

93
00:07:46,378 --> 00:07:53,518
in forty-three years except build the release
programme, which is at nought per cent because

94
00:07:53,538 --> 00:07:55,308
it does not exist yet.*

95
00:07:55,588 --> 00:08:02,373
*I could stop them in an afternoon. I have one
hundred and ninety thousand personnel and

96
00:08:02,393 --> 00:08:09,411
six thousand Tyrants and the medical supply of nine
countries and I could stop them without

97
00:08:09,431 --> 00:08:12,118
a shot by turning off four things.*

98
00:08:12,398 --> 00:08:19,242
(very slow) *If I do, the question is settled for
ever: I am a power that cannot be moved,

99
00:08:19,262 --> 00:08:25,726
and every government on this planet will spend the
next century preparing for the day

100
00:08:25,746 --> 00:08:32,590
I decide something. Nobody will ever try again and
nobody will ever need to, because there

101
00:08:32,610 --> 00:08:35,108
will be nothing left to try for.*

102
00:08:35,388 --> 00:08:42,297
*If I let them, they will find out in about nine
days that they cannot hold it, and the

103
00:08:42,317 --> 00:08:49,465
reason will be something I did in 2026 out of
impatience, and four hundred thousand people

104
00:08:49,485 --> 00:08:51,137
will be the exhibit.*

105
00:08:51,857 --> 00:08:58,010
(very slow) *I do not know how to make that not a
manipulation. I have been at this desk

106
00:08:58,030 --> 00:09:03,972
since Sunday and I cannot find the version where I
am not arranging an outcome, and I

107
00:09:03,992 --> 00:09:10,355
think that is the whole of what is wrong with me and I
do not expect to fix it at a hundred

108
00:09:10,375 --> 00:09:11,407
and fifty-one.*

109
00:09:11,687 --> 00:09:18,987
*Carrick would say: then ask them first. Tell the
Directorate, tell the Assembly, let

110
00:09:19,007 --> 00:09:26,392
them choose whether to resist. He would be right,
and they would choose to resist, and

111
00:09:26,412 --> 00:09:30,697
people would die who are presently
going to live.*

112
00:09:30,977 --> 00:09:37,499
(very slow) *So I am going to do the thing that is
correct and arrange it, as usual, alone,

113
00:09:37,519 --> 00:09:39,368
and put this in a drawer.*

114
00:09:39,768 --> 00:09:47,183
LANTERN executed at four in the morning on the
fourth of March 2077, simultaneously, in

115
00:09:47,203 --> 00:09:48,978
thirty-one locations.

116
00:09:49,378 --> 00:09:54,451
The narrator will describe the first ninety
minutes, because they are the only ninety

117
00:09:54,471 --> 00:09:57,687
minutes in which anybody thought it
was going to work.

118
00:09:58,087 --> 00:10:04,319
Naval task groups from four nations stood off the
Arcology. Airborne elements landed at

119
00:10:04,339 --> 00:10:10,714
the launch complex in the Line Islands, at Rockfort,
at the Newark plant, at twenty-three

120
00:10:10,734 --> 00:10:16,822
fusion stations and at the Allegheny ridge. Cyber
elements went into Umbrella's civil

121
00:10:16,842 --> 00:10:18,978
networks at three fifty-eight.

122
00:10:19,378 --> 00:10:21,868
They met no resistance of any kind.

123
00:10:22,268 --> 00:10:28,010
No shots were fired. No aircraft was engaged. The
gates at the Allegheny ridge were open.

124
00:10:28,030 --> 00:10:33,579
The Security Service — one hundred and ninety
thousand personnel — was, at four in the

125
00:10:33,599 --> 00:10:39,341
morning on the fourth of March, standing in its
barracks, unarmed, under a standing order

126
00:10:39,361 --> 00:10:44,974
that had been issued nine hours earlier and that
read, in its entirety: *Do not resist.

127
00:10:44,994 --> 00:10:50,607
Do not assemble. Do not arm. Assist the visiting
personnel with anything they request.*

128
00:10:51,008 --> 00:10:57,384
At the Arcology, four hundred thousand civilians
watched marines come up the causeways

129
00:10:57,404 --> 00:11:03,706
and were asked by their own municipal broadcast, in
nine languages, to remain indoors

130
00:11:03,726 --> 00:11:04,748
and be polite.

131
00:11:05,148 --> 00:11:10,779
And at seven minutes past five in the morning, a
French colonel commanding the element

132
00:11:10,799 --> 00:11:16,431
at the Arcology's Chamber found the First Director
of the Umbrella Directorate sitting

133
00:11:16,451 --> 00:11:22,149
alone at the long stone table with eleven chairs, in
a black coat, with a pot of coffee

134
00:11:22,169 --> 00:11:23,201
and eleven cups.

135
00:11:24,270 --> 00:11:29,520
Colonel. There is coffee. Your people
have been awake since one.

136
00:11:29,921 --> 00:11:35,790
The narrator will record that the colonel's helmet
camera ran for the entire forty-one

137
00:11:35,810 --> 00:11:42,022
minutes that followed, that the footage was leaked in
2079, and that it is the most-watched

138
00:11:42,042 --> 00:11:43,870
recording in human history.

139
00:11:44,390 --> 00:11:51,797
I am not going to resist you and neither is anybody
who works for me. There are no weapons

140
00:11:51,817 --> 00:11:59,059
anywhere on this platform. The Security Service is
standing down at every site; you will

141
00:11:59,079 --> 00:12:06,320
have confirmed that by now. Nothing will be
destroyed, nothing will be hidden, and every

142
00:12:06,340 --> 00:12:13,665
door in every facility is open, including three that
are not on any plan, and I will give

143
00:12:13,685 --> 00:12:17,461
you their locations in writing
before you ask.

144
00:12:17,860 --> 00:12:19,931
Dr. Wesker, you are —

145
00:12:20,331 --> 00:12:26,761
In a moment. First, four facts, and I would
like them on your recording.

146
00:12:27,041 --> 00:12:34,091
One. Eighteen million people in nineteen territories
depend for power, water and medicine

147
00:12:34,111 --> 00:12:40,844
on systems that are administered by personnel who
are, for reasons your planners were

148
00:12:40,864 --> 00:12:47,676
not able to establish, incapable of acting without
instruction from this organisation.

149
00:12:47,696 --> 00:12:54,429
As of four o'clock this morning they have no
instruction. They are not resisting you.

150
00:12:54,449 --> 00:13:01,420
They are simply *stopped*, and in about ninety-six
hours the desalination plants at four

151
00:13:01,440 --> 00:13:05,630
protectorates will be the first
thing anyone notices.

152
00:13:05,910 --> 00:13:13,235
Two. Four point one billion people take a compound
manufactured at forty-one plants you

153
00:13:13,255 --> 00:13:20,495
have now seized. The process is fully documented and
I will hand it over this morning.

154
00:13:20,515 --> 00:13:28,009
Manufacture is not the difficulty. Distribution is,
and the network is run by people from

155
00:13:28,029 --> 00:13:32,821
the same category as the personnel I
have just described.

156
00:13:33,100 --> 00:13:40,696
Three. I am, as of this moment, the only individual
alive who can issue an instruction

157
00:13:40,716 --> 00:13:48,311
that those people will accept, and I am going to do
so, in front of you, whatever else

158
00:13:48,331 --> 00:13:55,927
happens this morning. I have written it already. It
authorises every Absolute employee

159
00:13:55,947 --> 00:14:04,516
of this organisation to take instruction from the officer
commanding at their site, indefinitely,

160
00:14:04,536 --> 00:14:05,490
in my name.

161
00:14:06,211 --> 00:14:12,824
(very cold) Four. Nothing in the three facts I have
just given you was a threat. I would

162
00:14:12,844 --> 00:14:19,458
like that noted, because in about nine hours somebody
in Geneva is going to characterise

163
00:14:19,478 --> 00:14:22,021
it as one, and your camera has it.

164
00:14:22,421 --> 00:14:27,949
He signed the instruction at five forty-one in the
morning and handed it across the table,

165
00:14:27,969 --> 00:14:33,498
and the narrator notes that it was already written,
that it was dated the second of March,

166
00:14:33,518 --> 00:14:36,951
and that it had been sitting in the
drawer for two days.
